Vendored build inputs for the Ubuntu PPA source package
========================================================

Launchpad's PPA build farm has no outbound network access, so anything the
build needs must be shipped inside the source package. The two tarballs here
are git-ignored (too large for git) and must be in place before building the
source package. debian/rules extracts them into .flutter/ and .pub-cache/,
runs `flutter pub get --offline` and `flutter build linux --release --no-pub`,
and nothing reaches the network.

flutter-3.44.6-linux-slim.tar.xz
--------------------------------
A Linux-only slice of the Flutter 3.44.6 stable SDK (x64 engine only), about
147 MB. It is the same file SecureShell Go ships
(sha256 3d4277f96e83fc41f946f47ee7320565d77bf8760b36ae4607a8df8641c1e8eb);
its packaging/vendor/README lists what was pruned from the upstream tarball
and how to regenerate it for a new Flutter pin. Copy or hard-link it from
there rather than rebuilding it.

pub-cache-3.44.6.tar.xz
-----------------------
The pub.dev packages pinned by pubspec.lock (92 hosted packages) and their
hashes, about 37 MB. It goes stale whenever pubspec.lock changes: a package
added or upgraded since it was built makes `flutter pub get --offline` fail
with "could not find package <name> in cache". Rebuild it before a PPA upload
that follows a pubspec.lock change:

    S=$(mktemp -d); mkdir "$S/src"
    git archive HEAD | tar -x -C "$S/src"      # a clean checkout
    cd "$S/src"
    PUB_CACHE="$S/cache" flutter pub get --enforce-lockfile
    cd "$S/cache"
    tar --exclude='hosted/pub.dev/.cache' --owner=0 --group=0 --sort=name \
        -cf - hosted hosted-hashes | xz -6 -T0 \
        > <repo>/packaging/vendor/pub-cache-3.44.6.tar.xz

Rename both tarballs (and FLUTTER_VERSION / FLUTTER_ENGINE_VERSION in
debian/rules) when the Flutter pin in .github/workflows/ci.yml changes.
